# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and never committed.
#
# Two providers, both probed and both able to serve a vision call under a
# json_schema response format, which is what the extraction path requires.
# The custom profile leads and gemini is the spillover behind it, so a run
# survives one provider going down or running out of quota mid corpus.

# Primary. NVIDIA NIM serves an OpenAI compatible API, so it needs no code of
# its own: the custom profile is a base URL, a key, and a model name.
CROSSFOOT_LLM_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
CROSSFOOT_LLM_API_KEY=
CROSSFOOT_LLM_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-nano-12b-v2-vl
# NIM accepts a json_schema response format and answers a small schema, then
# returns 500 on the full document schema. Set this false to send the call
# without the format; the reply is validated on this side either way.
# CROSSFOOT_LLM_JSON_SCHEMA=false

# Fallback. Reads a scanned page about as well and has a much smaller free
# daily allowance, so it is the second profile rather than the first.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Any other OpenAI compatible endpoint works in the primary slot, a local
# Ollama included. Expect a small local model to read a heavy photocopy far
# worse than either of the above; the accuracy table in the README is per tier
# and shows how much the model choice is worth.

# Other settings:
# CROSSFOOT_LLM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120
# CROSSFOOT_DATA_DIR=data
